PATIENT EDUCATION

Treatment Explanation: A hormone called aldosterone is telling your kidneys to hold onto massive amounts of salt and water (causing the high blood pressure) and to dump all your potassium into your urine. The lack of potassium has essentially turned off the electrical signals to your leg muscles. The hospital will replace the potassium safely through a drip.
Actionable Steps: Stop taking the indapamide pill immediately. The adult child should gather all current medication boxes to show the emergency doctors. Rest quietly until the ambulance arrives.

